WEBVTT

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:08.650
All right...

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:10.650
Let's eat!

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:07.690
Summer's great, isn't it?

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:10.690
Yeah! Summer's the best!

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:25.500
I wanna slap myself for even thinking that.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:30.500
I wonder if it will cool down soon...

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:35.420
You're obviously just exhausted from the heat.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:41.510
I thought coming to school would be a good idea

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:43.890
because they usually crank the A/C up.

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:57.240
You really feel the temperature difference between inside and outside.

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:59.780
Just breathing makes me hot!

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:02.200
Ugh, I don't think I can stand any more of this air.

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:04.700
You'd die.

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:13.460
I really do wonder how we're going to make it through this summer.

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:16.420
You should eat well.

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:17.960
It will give you strength.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:20.260
I suppose you're right.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:22.760
Anyway, see you.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:25.300
See you tomorrow.

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:26.470
Kirin?

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:34.360
I guess I do have to breathe.

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:37.070
Gah, it's so hot!

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:39.070
You were serious about that?

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:44.410
I want something cold!

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:47.290
You just had a soda.

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:52.460
Having nothing but cold drinks will just make it worse on you.

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:56.840
It's also bad for your tummy.

00:03:56.840 --> 00:04:00.090
Why don't we have a nice meal instead?

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:05.470
But I can't think of anything I want...

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:08.100
Kirin, not hungry?

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:10.930
Hold on, where's my camera app...

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:12.100
Camera?

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:19.730
Sorry. I just never see you not hungry, so I wanted to take a picture.

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:29.950
My body is craving for something, but I can't figure out what.

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:31.700
Craving something?

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:33.460
Hmm...

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:37.210
I think what summer exhaustion calls for is something rich.

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.340
Perhaps eel?

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:40.090
Eel?

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:43.470
Ah, yes.

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:47.680
I guess eating it live would give you energy.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:49.470
That's a bit extreme.

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:53.980
But no! I mean eel bowl!

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:58.730
Eel bowl? You mean the stuff that gets served like in a jewelry box?

00:04:58.730 --> 00:04:59.820
Yep.

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:01.360
Eel!

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:05.070
I'm glad you have your appetite back.

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:08.830
We don't have eel often, so let's get good spices and rice too!

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:11.330
Sounds good!

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:18.210
Let's get real pickles too!

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:22.260
Nara pickles goes great with eel.

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:27.090
Ryo, look! They have a special rice display!

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:28.510
Oh, wow!

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:34.350
We'll need some Japanese pepper too.

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:36.600
Let's get something nice and spicy!

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:50.030
I forgot how exhausted I was.

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:56.960
The A/C inside was cranked up so high that the heat outside just drains all my energy away.

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:01.960
I can't take this anymore...

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:03.880
There.

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:10.470
Looks like the rice is done.

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:16.480
First we fill the box with fluffy, freshly-cooked rice.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:21.310
Then we cover it with warm kabayaki eel,

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:24.230
and then drizzle it with homemade sauce.

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:30.620
And it's done! An eel bowl that'll blow those summer doldrums away!

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:35.750
Sprinkle on a good amount of pepper, and...

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:37.750
It's time to eat!

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:55.010
The fluffy, savory meat is melting in my mouth!

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:03.690
The syrupy, sweet sauce is blending with the rice.

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:07.280
The eel is in-season, juicy, and sticky.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:18.410
This is way better than eating it raw!

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:22.420
You've never actually done that, right?

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:26.170
That was great.

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:29.300
Eel's wonderful in summer.

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:33.550
It didn't quite hit the spot though.

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:38.060
I mean, it was great, but that wasn't what I was really craving.

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:41.690
You too, Kirin? To be honest, I feel the same way.

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:45.270
It's not what my body was craving.

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:49.320
It's like there's some switch that it didn't flip...

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:52.240
What's wrong?

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:55.320
Isn't it kind of hot in here?

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:58.580
Hm? But I turned on the A/C...

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:00.830
Huh, it's not blowing.

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:05.540
I think it might be broken.

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:10.720
Wait, no way! There's no way it can break now!

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:13.590
I'm sweating all over now too!

00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:15.680
From the eel?

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:19.560
It flipped a different switch instead,
but now the A/C's switch isn't working!

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:21.060
It's too hot!

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:23.850
Let's wash the sweat off with a bath then!

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:28.900
Hurry, into the bath!

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:30.740
Quick!

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:35.200
There's no water.

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:38.240
I'll fill it up right away.

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:46.670
It's really hard to wait for the bath like this.

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:48.840
It's all muggy in here too.

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:51.510
Shall we step out for a minute?

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:55.590
I don't want to put those sweaty clothes back on.

00:08:55.890 --> 00:09:01.520
But if we don't bathe, we'll get our pajamas sweaty too.

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:04.190
So we just have to kill time until the bath fills.

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:06.020
How about we play Last and First?

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:07.440
That's a good idea.

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:10.150
Okay, I'll start.

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:11.860
Last and First!

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:12.860
Squirrels!

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:14.110
Sri Lanka!

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:16.110
Aromatic curry!

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:18.120
Yummy stew...

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:22.080
Ugh, too hot!

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:24.330
Just thinking about it warms me up!

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:26.170
We just made things worse...

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:32.340
The bath isn't full yet.

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:35.050
It's only about halfway.

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:40.510
Ugh, I can't take being drenched with sweat anymore!

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:42.470
Calm down, Kirin!

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:45.480
Let's play it again, except only with cold things this time.

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:47.310
Good idea.

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:49.650
I'll start, then.

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:51.400
Wait.

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:57.360
Maybe we should shower some of the sweat off before we bathe?

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:02.450
That sounds so obvious! Why didn't I think of that?

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:07.370
The heat is making it hard for you to even think.

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:10.960
Gotcha!

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:14.710
That was refreshing.

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:15.920
Yeah.

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:18.180
Yeah, it was, but...

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:21.300
There's still something missing.

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:22.350
The bathwater...

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:25.430
I'm getting in!

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:26.930
No fair!

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:29.690
It doesn't even come up to my shoulders.

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:31.860
I'm getting in too.

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:33.940
There's not enough room!

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:38.700
This is a nice bath.

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:42.620
Having both of us in here pushes up the water level.

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:47.540
So it's eco-friendly too.

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:50.370
Maybe we should do this every day.

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:53.540
...Nah, maybe not.

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:55.340
Yeah, maybe not.

00:10:59.340 --> 00:11:01.260
I think I'm getting dizzy.

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:03.390
Shall we get out?

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:06.430
I don't wanna. The A/C's still broken.

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:10.600
Now that I think of it, Grandma hated how the cold air coming from the A/C felt,

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:14.060
so we just used fans when I was little.

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:17.570
No A/C? That must've sucked!

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:21.030
It actually wasn't that bad.

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:25.700
It feels like summers were milder when I was—

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:27.580
It's just because you were young.

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:31.170
You can't just be energetic 24/7 anymore, Ryo.

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:34.960
I guess.

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:41.970
But the dark of the night sky was so cooling after a bath...

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:43.970
Ice cream,

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:46.970
a fan, and a hand fan...

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:49.100
The smell of a mosquito coil...

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:57.690
The ring of a wing chime that cools you off just by hearing it.

00:11:57.690 --> 00:11:58.690
That's it!

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:00.360
What, a wind chime?

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:01.570
No!

00:12:01.570 --> 00:12:03.660
Ryo, I want ice cream!

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:05.280
Right here, right now!

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:10.040
Ice cream, in the bath?
After what we just ate?

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:12.290
It's definitely ice cream!

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:16.670
That must be what we've been craving!

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:18.670
Are you sure?

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:21.840
Come on! I've always wanted to try ice cream in the bath!

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:22.970
Just imagine it!

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:24.220
But...

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:30.520
Imagine feeling the sweet, cold ice cream slide down your throat in a haze of steam!

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:36.110
It must be the ultimate relaxation as you sit in the bath!

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:47.660
Having ice cream in the bath must be like an oasis for the heart!

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:51.870
I suppose we have to try it now.

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:56.790
But just this once, okay?

00:12:56.790 --> 00:12:58.420
That's the spirit!

00:13:02.210 --> 00:13:04.510
Ice cream, ice cream...

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:09.180
Wait, why did I decide this was a good idea?

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:12.930
I feel like Kirin's manipulating me.

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:16.770
Ah, I'm getting water all over the floor!

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:22.280
I'm going to have to make Kirin help clean up later.

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:26.160
Ah...

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:31.290
The cool air of the freezer feels so good on my moist skin...

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:36.000
Oh no! This will run up the power bill!

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:39.000
Wait, I forgot the ice cream.

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:44.670
This is so bad, but it feels so good.

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:47.220
<i>I'm sorry, Grandma.</i>

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:50.220
<i>I think I'm becoming a bad girl.</i>

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:51.600
What are you doing?

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:56.560
Kirin, I, uh...

00:13:56.560 --> 00:14:00.480
You took so long that I came to get some myself.

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:02.440
Wait, Ryo, look out!

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:03.820
The curtains are open!

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:07.610
It's fine. The lights across the street are already out.

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:12.740
That doesn't matter! Someone could be peeping on us with a telescope!

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:14.830
Kirin?

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:16.620
Don't worry, Ryo! I'll protect you!

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:21.290
I'm flat, so it's not as big of a deal if someone sees me!

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:26.630
Kirin... Thank you. I think.

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:28.470
You're welcome.

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:32.010
Now I'm hot again.

00:14:32.010 --> 00:14:34.180
Let's have that ice cream.

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:40.270
Hurry! Hurry!

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:42.520
It's melting!

00:14:42.520 --> 00:14:44.860
Slow down a little, Kirin.

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:49.110
All right...

00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:51.120
Let's eat!

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:13.550
The coolness of the vanilla is spreading through my mouth.

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:15.390
It feels so good.

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:24.480
These popsicles are so much lighter than normal vanilla ice cream.

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:28.650
The sweetness reminds me a bit of the old days.

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:31.160
Kyaa, I'm getting brain freeze!

00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:36.240
Eating ice cream in the bath feels so luxurious.

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:41.420
But it melts fast.

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:43.420
Well, this <i>is</i> the bath.

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:48.260
On the other hand, it's convenient. We can just wash it off right here.

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:52.260
It's not like it was designed to be eaten in the bath.

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:55.390
I'm refreshed.

00:15:55.760 --> 00:15:58.310
That was a pretty long bath.

00:15:58.310 --> 00:16:02.020
Though I guess we did take a break halfway.

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:04.560
So, was that it?

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:07.770
Was ice cream what you were craving?

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:10.490
I dunno...

00:16:10.490 --> 00:16:12.610
So it wasn't?

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:17.620
I don't feel as exhausted anymore, but...

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:20.580
I'm not quite sure either.

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:23.620
There's still <i>something...</i>

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:25.080
Rice-flour dumplings?

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:28.920
No, maybe strawberry buns?

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:32.590
That paleness, that perky, springy feel...

00:16:34.090 --> 00:16:36.680
Why are you staring <i>there</i> when you say that?!

00:16:36.680 --> 00:16:37.850
Stop it!

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:45.650
I don't think those buns would be enough to satisfy me though.

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:48.860
What are you implying?! I don't have to take this!

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:52.280
It's not quite what I'm looking for.

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:57.370
This is it!

00:16:57.370 --> 00:16:59.160
A can of red beans?

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:02.580
Wait, you want a red bean sundae?

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:05.960
We still have a bit of that mochi that was on sale left over, right?

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:08.750
I guess?

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:10.420
So make red bean soup for me!

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:15.050
Found it!

00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:20.100
Ryo, I'm plugging it in!

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:22.270
Okay.

00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:29.940
Hey, this isn't half-bad.

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:32.030
It's done!

00:17:33.150 --> 00:17:35.280
Is this what you wanted?

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:37.740
Thanks, Ryo!

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:39.660
Chow time!

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:44.870
This really isn't the season for red bean soup. I never would have thought to cook it myself.

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:47.370
I'm not sure if it's good for your tummy...

00:17:49.630 --> 00:17:50.670
This is it!

00:17:50.670 --> 00:17:53.670
I've been craving sweet beans like this!

00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:55.970
The mochi's nice and stretchy too.

00:17:58.010 --> 00:18:02.100
This is what I've been craving!

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:07.480
<i>So it didn't have anything to do with the weather or heat exhaustion.</i>

00:18:10.190 --> 00:18:11.820
Aren't you going to have some?

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:15.240
Seriously, Kirin? Red bean soup in summer?

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:18.660
It's tasty enough to eat all year round!

00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:24.870
<i>Get serious, Ryo!</i>

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:29.580
<i>It's mid-summer, and you've already had eel bowl and ice cream!</i>

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:31.840
<i>This is terrible for you!</i>

00:18:31.840 --> 00:18:32.710
<i>That said...</i>

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:39.010
I... I guess I will.

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:41.260
No time like the present!

00:18:43.890 --> 00:18:46.020
<i>I'm such a fool...</i>

00:18:55.400 --> 00:18:56.570
This is...

00:18:57.150 --> 00:18:58.610
Great!

00:18:58.610 --> 00:19:03.530
The gentle sweetness of the red bean paste soothes my heart.

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:12.000
The unique sensation of steamy-warm red beans and mochi on a hot day...

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:15.380
I think this might be what we were craving.

00:19:15.960 --> 00:19:18.380
Yeah! Totally!

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:23.890
I might've bought a bit too much.

00:19:29.350 --> 00:19:30.640
Who is it?

00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:34.820
It's Shiina. I bought some refreshing food.

00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:37.440
How are you two feeling?

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:39.400
Shiina! Great timing!

00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:43.870
Help me! Ryo's in trouble!

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:48.870
<i>Her condition's deteriorated.</i>

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:53.880
So you had eel bowl, ice cream, and red bean soup all in one meal?

00:19:54.210 --> 00:19:57.460
Sorry to make you worry...

00:19:57.750 --> 00:19:59.840
Those just don't go together!

00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:02.510
Of course they'd make you sick.

00:20:02.510 --> 00:20:05.720
And you still finished them all?

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:10.230
They were so tasty, and Kirin lured me in...

00:20:10.520 --> 00:20:14.860
You need to watch out. You're not Morino. You don't have a stomach of steel.

00:20:14.860 --> 00:20:16.610
Aw, shucks.

00:20:16.610 --> 00:20:18.360
That wasn't a compliment.

00:20:18.360 --> 00:20:21.570
Anyway, Ryo, you should get some rest.

00:20:21.570 --> 00:20:22.860
I've laid out your mattress.

00:20:23.820 --> 00:20:27.830
Thanks... For everything...

00:20:33.870 --> 00:20:35.580
Good night, Ryo.

00:20:38.550 --> 00:20:40.510
So, is there any red bean soup left?

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:42.760
I want some too now.

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:14.250
<i>Grandma...</i>

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:21.300
Ryo's smiling.

00:21:30.970 --> 00:21:35.940
I guess sitting around like this does cool you off.

00:21:37.400 --> 00:21:38.310
Ryo...

00:21:46.910 --> 00:21:50.200
Ugh, too much red bean soup.

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:52.450
I'm burning up inside...

00:21:54.960 --> 00:21:57.870
Hey, let's get something to eat on the way home.

00:21:57.870 --> 00:22:03.710
In hot weather like this, curry or spicy ramen would—

00:23:40.850 --> 00:23:43.940
Huh, Kirin? Don't you eat the middle?

00:23:43.940 --> 00:23:51.570
Huh? Well, I love the outside, but the middle's all bitter and nasty....

00:23:51.570 --> 00:23:52.990
But that's such a waste!

00:23:52.990 --> 00:23:54.820
It's best when you eat it all at once.

00:23:54.820 --> 00:23:58.370
Now, open wide and say "ah"!

00:24:00.040 --> 00:24:03.210
Ryo, you're normally not mean like this!

00:24:03.210 --> 00:24:05.750
Next on Gourmet Girl Graffiti:

00:24:05.750 --> 00:24:07.880
Sizzling and Popping!
